	[This is a visual map file for the game savage empire in
	 .GIF format. I debated whether to post this or not because
	 it's not really "source" per se, but it's not clear where
	 else would be an appropriate place to post it. Also, it is
	 not just PC specific in that GIF files can also be viewed
	 with several X windows tools (e.g. xloadimage).
	 There are three (3) .uu? files that should be unpacked,
	 concatenated and feed to uudecode(1).  -br]

#! /bin/sh
# This is a shell archive.  Remove anything before this line, then unpack
# it by saving it into a file and typing "sh file".  To overwrite existing
# files, type "sh file -c".  You can also feed this as standard input via
# unshar, or by typing "sh <file", e.g..  If this archive is complete, you
# will see the following message at the end:
#		"End of archive 1 (of 3)."
# Contents:  README MANIFEST savagmap.uub
# Wrapped by billr@saab on Fri Dec  7 15:05:11 1990
PATH=/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/ucb ; export PATH
if test -f 'README' -a "${1}" != "-c" ; then 
  echo shar: Will not clobber existing file \"'README'\"
else
echo shar: Extracting \"'README'\" \(528 characters\)
sed "s/^X//" >'README' <<'END_OF_FILE'
XPlaying Savage Empire without a map?  Well no more!
X
XThis is a very detailed overland map of the game Savage Empire.
X
XI worked many hours reverse engineering the data files and have discovered
Xtheir format and am making it available to everyone here.
X
XPLEASE NOTE: This map is what many would consider a MAJOR SPOILER, so use
Xyour own judgement. 
X
XThe map is 1024 x 1024 x 16 and is in the GIF format.
X
XBTW, I also have similar maps to Ultima 5 and Ultima 6 if anyone's interested.
X
XEnjoy.
X
XGerhard Karnik
Xgaryk@cbnewsk.att.COM
END_OF_FILE
if test 528 -ne `wc -c <'README'`; then
    echo shar: \"'README'\" unpacked with wrong size!
fi
# end of 'README'
fi
if test -f 'MANIFEST' -a "${1}" != "-c" ; then 
  echo shar: Will not clobber existing file \"'MANIFEST'\"
else
echo shar: Extracting \"'MANIFEST'\" \(269 characters\)
sed "s/^X//" >'MANIFEST' <<'END_OF_FILE'
X   File Name		Archive #	Description
X-----------------------------------------------------------
X MANIFEST                   1	This shipping list
X README                     1	
X savagmap.uua               2	
X savagmap.uub               1	
X savagmap.uuc               3	
END_OF_FILE
if test 269 -ne `wc -c <'MANIFEST'`; then
    echo shar: \"'MANIFEST'\" unpacked with wrong size!
fi
# end of 'MANIFEST'
fi
if test -f 'savagmap.uub' -a "${1}" != "-c" ; then 
  echo shar: Will not clobber existing file \"'savagmap.uub'\"
else
echo shar: Extracting \"'savagmap.uub'\" \(56420 characters\)
